From 3b6b5c57f5d4ee34b2765d9940a7de89b6d58fbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:43:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep root shell comments out of lifecycle output
 sinks

Raw sink regexes treated semicolons and backticks inside shell comments as executed command substitutions, promoting unrelated quoted data paths into script traversal. Mask only proven full-line root comments; preserve quoted/interpreter source and opaque expansions/groups, and abandon masking on unsupported or incomplete regions. Only simply quoted heredoc delimiters are traversed; unquoted backslash-newline delimiter joins remain conservative.

Proof: original minimal and oversized-data wrapper assertions fail without integration (20 failures); 29 importing/cross-cutting suites pass 3133 tests, scripts/check passes 20 checks. Real Bash markers cover inert comments, real substitutions and unquoted heredoc false closes; 48 generated wrapper/nesting cases retain baseline refusals. All 31 condition/integration mutants killed. Read-only real-row replay running separately before ship.
